    You ask <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> about his opinion of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> and he laughs. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span>? Why does he interest you, I wonder? If you must know, he is nothing but gutter trash too stupid to know his place. We can only hope that he realizes what he is and takes himself out with the garbage, so to speak.”</span> <br>
    <br>
<<else>>
    You ask <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> about his opinion of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> and he laughs. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“A useless waste of space that should do the world a favor and take himself out like the trash that he is.”</span> <span style="color:Yellow">You are a bit stunned by his direct choice of words.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Should hardly be a surprise. I love my toys, even ones with little use, but I’d rather see <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> hurt than embarrassed.”</span> <span style="color:Yellow">He reads your face, trying to gauge your reaction to his harsh words.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Hope that doesn’t change your opinion of me.”</span> He smiles. <br>
    <br>
<</if>><br>
<br>
<<endByLocation>>

